==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* '''[[chock-a-block]]'''
* '''chock a block'''

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-chockablock.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{nautical}} (of a ship's [[hoist]]ing [[tackle]]) Having the [[block]]s drawn close together so no further [[movement]] is possible, as when the tackle is [[haul]]ed to the utmost.
# {{by extension}} [[jammed|Jammed]] [[tightly]] together; very [[crowded]]; completely [[filled]] or [[stuffed]].
#: ''Some of Sardinia's gorgeous seaside towns have lately been invaded by builders who erected '''chockablock''' housing that catered to middle-income tourists but threatened to spoil the landscape.''

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[crowded]] manner; as [[completely]] or [[closely]] as possible.
#: ''His study had books stacked '''chockablock''' on every shelf.''
#: ''The meeting hall was '''chockablock''' full of angry citizens.''

===Related terms===
